---
import ArticleLayout from '../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import { getDocumentationSidebar } from '../../data/nav';
---
<ArticleLayout
  title="Documentation"
  section="documentation"
  description="Standards and guidelines for how and when to use the design system."
  pageTitle="Get started"
  pageSubtitle="Adopt the GovBB Design System in a new or existing government service."
  sidebarGroups={await getDocumentationSidebar()}
  sidebarLabel="Get started"
>
  <div class="govbb-prose">
    <p>
      The system is for designers, developers and service teams across government.
      Follow these steps to use a shared foundation without losing sight of the user task.
    </p>
    <ol class="govbb-step-list">
      <li>
        <h2>Understand the standards</h2>
        <p>Start with the accessibility, token and component requirements every service follows.</p>
        <a href="/documentation/using-the-design-system/#standards">Read the standards</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h2>Choose the right level</h2>
        <p>Use styles for foundations, components for interface parts, patterns for tasks and templates for whole pages.</p>
        <a href="/documentation/using-the-design-system/#guidelines">Understand the guidance</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h2>Install and build</h2>
        <p>Use the frontend package for CSS and tokens, or the React package when your service uses React.</p>
        <a href="/documentation/using-the-design-system/">Use the design system</a>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</ArticleLayout>
